{"shortDescription":"The Australian dollar steadied around $0.71, holding recent losses as investors assessed stronger-than-expected GDP data that strengthened the case for another interest rate hike.The economy expanded 0.4% quarter-on-quarter in Q2, beating forecasts for 0.3% growth, while annual growth accelerated t…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The Australian dollar steadied around $0.71, holding recent losses as investors assessed stronger-than-expected GDP data that strengthened the case for another interest rate hike."]},{"type":"p","children":["The economy expanded 0.4% quarter-on-quarter in Q2, beating forecasts for 0.3% growth, while annual growth accelerated to 2.1%, above expectations for 1.8%."]},{"type":"p","children":["The stronger reading suggested economic activity remains resilient despite the Reserve Bank's efforts to cool demand and curb persistent inflation."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets raised the odds of a fourth rate hike at the September meeting to 57% from 48% previously after the GDP release, while a November hike is now more than fully priced in."]},{"type":"p","children":["The probability of another hike in Q1 2027 also rose to 82% from 62%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, concerns over potential oil supply disruptions amid the escalating US-Iran conflict have pushed energy prices higher, adding to inflation pressures."]},{"type":"p","children":["However, a stronger US dollar capped the Aussie as rising yields boosted demand for safe-haven currencies."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:580275:0","title":"Aussie Dollar Steadies After Strong GDP Data","published":1788315758,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/australia/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:AUDUSD","currency-logoid":"country/US",